Hierarchy
Browser
   └── BrowserContext
            └── Page

1. Browser

A Browser is the actual browser instance launched by Playwright.

Examples:

Chromium
Firefox
WebKit

It is the top-level object
Responsibilities
Launch browser
Close browser
Manage contexts
Browser browser = playwright.chromium().launch();
This launches browser.

2. BrowserContext

A BrowserContext is an isolated browser session inside the browser.

Like:

Incognito window
Separate user session

Each context has:

separate cookies
separate local storage
separate login session
Responsibilities
Session isolation
Multi-user testing
Parallel execution
Java Example
BrowserContext context = browser.newContext();
3. Page

A Page represents a single tab/window inside a BrowserContext.

This is where actual automation happens.

Responsibilities
Click
Type
Navigate
Validate UI
Java Example
Page page = context.newPage();
