“Browser is the actual browser instance managed by Playwright. BrowserContext is an isolated 
session within the browser that maintains separate authentication and storage states. 
Page represents a single tab inside a context where UI interactions are performed. 
This layered architecture helps Playwright support efficient parallel execution and multi-user testing.”
